      '<h3>How it works</h3>',
      'Required columns are <code>ticker</code>, <code>shares</code> and <code>avg_cost</code>. Optional columns are <code>name</code>, <code>sector</code> and <code>notes</code>. Header names are matched without regard to capitalization or surrounding spaces. Each file can hold up to 1,000 rows.',
      'Every row is checked on its own. A row is skipped if the ticker is missing or badly formed (letters, digits, dots and hyphens, up to 12 characters), if <code>shares</code> is not a number greater than zero, or if <code>avg_cost</code> is not a number of zero or more. The ticker check is a format check only: it does not confirm the symbol trades on an exchange. Valid rows are imported even when others are skipped.',
      'Nothing is written at all if a required column is missing, the file is empty or cannot be read as CSV, it has more than 1,000 rows, or no row passes validation. Imported rows are added to the team portfolio as new positions; they do not replace or merge with positions already there.',
      '<h3>Troubleshooting</h3>',
